    "question": {
      ":question/id": "92f1374a-897d-5571-be36-85b2d9137a06",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since coefficient row $1$ contains only zeros, but row $2$ is nonzero (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 6 & 1 & 10 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $2$ is in the same column as the leading entry in row $1$, column $2$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 6 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 8 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $A$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
