  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129113,
      "id": "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3",
      "title": "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d819ca4b-ca80-5823-8d92-4b7b2a334b34",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 11 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -5 & 7 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & -7 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & 6 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $1$ is to the left of the leading entry in row $1$, column $3$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 11 & -9 \\\\ 9 & -5 & 7 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}6 & -7 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $B$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "06d96b44-b6a9-5648-bbd5-6ebaa5246bcd",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "48e1255c-3695-566c-abb8-033b7c5826c6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$A$ and $B$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7d36bdb0-6d55-5179-90ec-d912247d832b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$B$ and $C$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "25af3ab8-e3bc-5613-9ba3-c74b77bd774c",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$B$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9a2b9cee-82d3-5653-ba1f-b4c098c481dc",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$C$ only"
            },
